# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================

# DATA GOVERNANCE PRINCIPLE

# =============================================================================

This phase certifies one architectural question:

**Can Gordon identify, classify, govern, protect, trace, retain and safely
dispose of every piece of information throughout its entire lifecycle while
preserving integrity, provenance, privacy and architectural ownership?**

Information shall be treated as a first-class architectural asset.

Recover the complete repository information architecture including:

data authorities

information ownership

data governance

metadata

classification

provenance

privacy

confidentiality

retention

archival

deletion

lineage

traceability

knowledge ownership

memory ownership

checkpoint ownership

configuration ownership

audit ownership

artifact ownership

dataset governance

model provenance

information lifecycle

# =============================================================================

