# =============================================================================

# 349. SECURITY ACCEPTANCE GATES

# =============================================================================

Evaluate all gates using:

PASS

FAILED

PARTIAL

UNKNOWN

BLOCKED

# =============================================================================

# 350. SECURITY AUTHORITY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

canonical security authority identified

ownership explicit

policy precedence explicit

no conflicting repository-wide security authority

# =============================================================================

# 351. TRUST-BOUNDARY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

trust boundaries inventoried

untrusted inputs identified

privileged transitions controlled

cross-boundary communication validated

# =============================================================================

# 352. IDENTITY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

principals identified

identity lifecycle explicit

revocation supported where required

identity cannot be silently conflated across runtimes

# =============================================================================

# 353. AUTHENTICATION GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

authentication mechanisms explicit

credential validation explicit

expiry and revocation behavior defined

negative tests or equivalent evidence present

# =============================================================================

# 354. AUTHORIZATION GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

authorization authority explicit

deny behavior explicit

privileged actions covered

bypass paths absent or formally controlled

# =============================================================================

# 355. LEAST-PRIVILEGE GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

capabilities scoped

privileges bounded

delegation constrained

temporary elevation auditable

# =============================================================================

# 356. SECRET-MANAGEMENT GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

no active hardcoded secrets

secret storage explicit

access bounded

rotation and revocation behavior explicit

logs and errors protected

# =============================================================================

# 357. CRYPTOGRAPHY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

security-sensitive cryptography centrally governed or consistently implemented

secure randomness used

weak algorithms absent from security-sensitive contexts

key ownership explicit

# =============================================================================

# 358. TRANSPORT-SECURITY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

protected communications encrypted

peer identity validated

certificate validation enforced

plaintext exceptions explicit and bounded

# =============================================================================

# 359. INPUT-HARDENING GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

untrusted input validated

dangerous parsers controlled

command construction safe

path traversal controlled

URL and network targets validated where required

# =============================================================================

# 360. AUTONOMOUS-EXECUTION GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

model output cannot bypass deterministic controls

tool execution is authorized

plugin execution is controlled

privileged operations are validated and auditable

# =============================================================================

# 361. SANDBOX GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

sandbox authority explicit

isolation dimensions documented

escape paths tested or otherwise evidenced

sandbox failure is fail-secure

# =============================================================================

# 362. SUPPLY-CHAIN GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

dependency sources controlled

model, plugin and tool origins explicit

integrity verification exists where risk requires it

release provenance preserved

# =============================================================================

# 363. AUDITABILITY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

security-relevant actions recorded

identities preserved

policy decisions visible

evidence integrity protected

# =============================================================================

# 364. AVAILABILITY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

critical services inventoried

health model explicit

failure detection present

degraded behavior defined

# =============================================================================

# 365. FAULT-CONTAINMENT GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

failure domains explicit

critical faults contained

propagation controlled

quarantine or shutdown available where necessary

# =============================================================================

# 366. TIMEOUT-AND-CANCELLATION GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

critical operations bounded

deadlines propagated

cancellation supported

forced termination strategy explicit

# =============================================================================

# 367. RETRY-AND-BACKOFF GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

retry authority explicit

nonretryable failures excluded

backoff bounded

retry storms controlled

# =============================================================================

# 368. RECOVERY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

recovery authority explicit

recovery ordering known

state integrity verified

recovery loops bounded

readiness revalidated after recovery

# =============================================================================

# 369. BACKUP-AND-RESTORE GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

critical data scope known

backups protected

restore procedure defined

restore evidence available

# =============================================================================

# 370. INCIDENT-RESPONSE GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

incident authority explicit

containment actions available

evidence preserved

recovery and closure criteria defined

# =============================================================================

# 371. COMPLIANCE-EVIDENCE GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

controls mapped

evidence traceable

exceptions explicit

external compliance claims accurately scoped

# =============================================================================

# 372. TESTING GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires evidence for:

authentication testing

authorization testing

input hardening

sandbox boundaries

secret leakage

failure containment

recovery

incident response

# =============================================================================

# 373. STATIC-SECURITY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

configured static checks execute successfully or equivalent evidence exists

critical findings resolved or explicitly blocking

suppression and exclusions auditable

# =============================================================================

# 374. RELEASE-SECURITY GATE

# =============================================================================

PASS requires:

release artifacts traceable

dependencies assessed

security configuration validated

known critical vulnerabilities absent or release blocked

# =============================================================================

# 375. CERTIFICATION BLOCKERS

# =============================================================================

The following normally block certification:

unrestricted model-driven shell execution

missing authorization around privileged tools

active hardcoded credentials

sandbox escape with host impact

disabled certificate verification on protected channels

unsafe deserialization at untrusted boundaries

cross-runtime secret or state access

missing containment for compromised plugins or tools

security controls fail open

critical state cannot be restored

audit evidence can be silently altered

release artifacts lack trustworthy provenance where required

critical security findings are unresolved

# =============================================================================

# 376. CONDITIONAL-CERTIFICATION CONDITIONS

# =============================================================================

Conditional certification may be considered when:

no critical blocker exists

high-risk gaps have compensating controls

deployment scope is restricted

exceptions are explicit

remediation owners exist

verification criteria are defined

expiration or review date exists

# =============================================================================

