PROFILE-B

Local network, authenticated operators

PROFILE-C

Internet-exposed service

PROFILE-D

Multi-user or multi-tenant service

PROFILE-E

Distributed cluster

PROFILE-F

Autonomous privileged execution

Do not apply a single certification outcome to materially different deployment
profiles without explicit justification.

# =============================================================================

# 395. SECURITY CERTIFICATION DECISION

# =============================================================================

Allowed decisions:

CERTIFIED

CONDITIONALLY CERTIFIED

NOT CERTIFIED

UNABLE TO CERTIFY

The decision shall state:

scope

deployment profile

repository revision

evidence basis

passed gates

failed gates

partial gates

unknown gates

blockers

conditions

residual risks

confidence

# =============================================================================

# 396. CERTIFIED

# =============================================================================

Use only when:

all mandatory gates pass

no unresolved critical or blocking high-severity finding remains

evidence is sufficient

scope is explicit

residual risks are accepted by the appropriate authority

# =============================================================================

# 397. CONDITIONALLY CERTIFIED

# =============================================================================

Use only when:

no critical blocker remains

failed or partial gates are bounded

compensating controls exist

deployment restrictions are explicit

remediation conditions are testable

review or expiration is specified

# =============================================================================

# 398. NOT CERTIFIED

# =============================================================================

Use when:

mandatory gates fail

critical blockers exist

security controls are structurally absent

recovery is unsafe

autonomous privileged execution is insufficiently constrained

# =============================================================================

# 399. UNABLE TO CERTIFY

# =============================================================================

Use when:

repository evidence is insufficient

critical runtime behavior cannot be verified

required files are unavailable

test evidence is missing or unusable

scope cannot be determined

Do not convert insufficient evidence into a passing or failing implementation
claim.

