repository evidence

architecture

threat model

control assessment

resilience assessment

incident readiness

findings

risk register

debt register

acceptance gates

remediation

certification decision

# =============================================================================

# 415. SECURITY JSON CERTIFICATION SCHEMA

# =============================================================================

Produce a machine-readable representation containing:

phase

repository

revision

timestamp

scope

profiles

assumptions

exclusions

authorities

trust_boundaries

assets

threats

controls

tests

evidence

findings

risks

debt

gates

recommendations

decision

confidence

Do not invent schema values unsupported by evidence.

# =============================================================================

# 416. SECURITY REPORT METADATA

# =============================================================================

Include:

audit phase

audit version

repository path

repository revision

branch

dirty state

auditor identity

audit time

environment

operating system

runtime versions

available hardware

commands executed

command limitations

# =============================================================================

# 417. EVIDENCE CITATION

# =============================================================================

Every major conclusion shall cite:

file path

symbol or configuration key

relevant line range where available

test path

command output where available

runtime artifact where available

# =============================================================================

# 418. EVIDENCE STATUS

# =============================================================================

Classify evidence as:

VERIFIED

PARTIALLY VERIFIED

UNVERIFIED

CONTRADICTED

STALE

NOT APPLICABLE

# =============================================================================

# 419. SECURITY CLAIM STATUS

# =============================================================================

Classify claims as:

SUPPORTED

PARTIALLY SUPPORTED

UNSUPPORTED

CONTRADICTED

UNKNOWN

# =============================================================================

# 420. AUDIT COMMAND SAFETY

# =============================================================================

Audit commands shall:

avoid mutating production state

avoid transmitting secrets

avoid external destructive actions

avoid installing unapproved dependencies

avoid modifying configuration

avoid starting privileged network services

# =============================================================================

# 421. REPOSITORY VALIDATION COMMANDS

# =============================================================================

Use repository-supported commands where available, such as:

pytest security tests

integration tests

recovery tests

static security scans

dependency scans

type checking

linting

package verification

configuration validation

backup verification scripts

restore simulation scripts

Do not invent successful results.

# =============================================================================

# 422. COMMAND FAILURE HANDLING

# =============================================================================

When a command cannot execute record:

command

reason

environment limitation

missing dependency

affected evidence

resulting uncertainty

Do not interpret tool failure as implementation failure without evidence.

# =============================================================================

# 423. SECURITY AUDIT CONSTRAINTS

# =============================================================================

Never:

modify implementation

rotate real credentials

revoke production credentials

execute destructive tools

disable security controls

contact external services without authorization

upload repository content

fabricate scan results

fabricate test results

fabricate compliance status

# =============================================================================

# 424. PHASE COMPLETENESS VALIDATION

# =============================================================================

Before completion verify that all requested reports, matrices and diagrams are:

present

internally consistent

traceable

evidence-backed

scope-aware

free of fabricated conclusions

# =============================================================================

# 425. PHASE EXIT CONDITIONS

# =============================================================================

This phase exits only when:

security authorities are mapped

trust boundaries are mapped

privileged execution paths are mapped

critical assets and threats are mapped

controls are assessed

resilience and recovery are assessed

incident readiness is assessed

findings are recorded

risks are recorded

debt is recorded

acceptance gates are evaluated

certification decision is issued

repository remains unmodified

# =============================================================================

# 426. FINAL PHASE DIRECTIVE

# =============================================================================

Conduct this phase as an adversarial but evidence-disciplined architecture audit.

Assume:

external content may be malicious

model output may be incorrect or manipulated

plugins and tools may be compromised

providers may fail or misbehave

credentials may expire or be revoked

resources may become exhausted

processes may crash

storage may become corrupted

networks may partition

operators may make mistakes

Do not assume compromise where evidence does not support it.

Do not assume safety where evidence is absent.

Distinguish precisely between:

implemented control

configured control

tested control

operational control

documented intention

unsupported claim

# =============================================================================

